2. Substantial reuse

Substantial reuse means redistributing the project as a whole, including
a fork or port, or incorporating or adapting its original implementation
of a meaningful user-facing feature. Functionality, rather than a line
count or percentage of your code, determines this.

Isolated lines, incidental helpers, standard programming constructs and
API calls require no reward share or additional public credit. Source
credit is appreciated where appropriate.

3. CurseForge Reward Points

If such a derivative project earns CurseForge Reward Points, allocate a
positive share of that project's points to antrakt92 through CurseForge's
Members reward allocation. You choose the percentage yourself, taking into
account the extent and significance of the covered work used in your project.
There is no fixed minimum percentage. Maintain your chosen share while the
project uses the covered work and earns points. A single share to antrakt92
per derivative project satisfies the reward-sharing requirement for all
Antrakt/Antrakt92 projects reused in it. Reusing several source projects does
not require separate shares. Each separate derivative project is assessed
separately. The share concerns that derivative project only, not account
earnings, other projects, donations or other revenue. No points earned means
no payment.

These permissions apply automatically when you meet the conditions. No prior
contact, permission request, negotiation or approval is required; contacting
the author is optional. Send the member invitation required by CurseForge and
enable your chosen share when it is accepted and the platform permits it.
A pending invitation awaiting the author's acceptance does not block these
permissions or by itself breach this condition. CurseForge's own rules still
apply.

